    Greek Archaeological Service from 1957 — and I have kept all three as it
    gives them rather than reconciling them. Two smaller notes: the lead and
    the History section point the same names at different link targets
    (archelaus-i-of-macedon against archelaus-of-macedon, aegae-macedonia
    against aegae-macedon, roman-republic against ancient-rome), and I copied
    each across unchanged rather than picking one; and only two of the corpus
    articles could be justified from this document, so \"further\" has two
